Crash was real and reproducible — I found and fixed it, then restyled the UI along Dolphin's lines.

**The crash.** History entries were created with a NULL title whenever a page had no `<title>`; opening the History panel then dereferenced it. Reproduced deterministically under gdb with a local page that has no title:

```
SIGSEGV in rebuild_history at menu.c:201
const char *title = *entry->title != '\0' ? entry->title : entry->url;
```

[history.c](src/history.c) now always gives an entry a title (empty string when the page has none), and [menu.c](src/menu.c) falls back to the URL defensively — untitled pages simply list their URL. I also fixed a latent use-after-free in the same panel: **Clear History** rebuilt the container that held the button currently being clicked; the button now lives in a persistent footer below the scrolling list, and clearing only replaces rows.

**UI, following your Dolphin screenshots.** A small GTK stylesheet in [browser.c](src/browser.c) (no extra toolkit, no custom drawing) plus class names gives:

- **Tabs** like Dolphin's: filled, rounded top corners, a gap between tabs, an accent-tinted checked tab with a 2px accent line along its top, hover lightening on inactive tabs, and a tinted tab strip that is visually separated from the page.
- **Toolbar** like Dolphin's: compact flat icon buttons, and the address field as a bordered rounded rectangle with a dark fill that takes the accent colour when focused, with the search glyph inside.
- **History panel** like Dolphin's menu: icon + title + dim subtitle rows, section labels, a divider, and the footer action. The main menu keeps its icon rows with right-side chevrons.

![Indigo main window](screenshots/ui-final.png)

![Three tabs](screenshots/ui-tabs2.png)

![History panel](screenshots/ui-history-final.png)

**Validation.** The untitled-page probe that crashed now runs clean; a stress harness driving the real handlers (menu → History, Clear History, history-row navigation, Settings, new tabs, closing tabs) ran 64 rounds with no crash and clearing left the history file at 0 bytes; `meson compile` and a strict `-Wall -Wextra -Werror` build are clean; a native session launch produced no warnings and stayed up.

**One caveat on the log you pasted:** `GtkGizmo … (slider) reported min width -2` is a GTK 4.22 bug, not ours — a 40-line test app with a popover containing a scrolled window prints the same two warnings here. Ignoring them is safe; they appear whenever a popover list is shown. The `Error releasing name … WebProcess` lines are normal web-process teardown when tabs close.

Files: [browser.c](src/browser.c), [menu.c](src/menu.c), [history.c](src/history.c), [pages.c](src/pages.c), plus [util.c](src/util.c)/[util.h](src/util.h) from the previous pass. `screenshots/` holds just the three images above; delete it if you don't want them in the tree.
