You were right — I was overriding the theme with hand-written CSS instead of using GTK. I removed all of it.

**What changed**

- **No stylesheet, no custom CSS classes.** [browser.c](src/browser.c) no longer loads any `GtkCssProvider`, and the `toolbar`/`address`/`tab-label`/`tab-close` classes are gone. Tabs are plain `GtkNotebook` tabs with the theme's own geometry, the entry is an ordinary `GtkEntry`, and spacing is GTK's default 6px margins / 4px gaps. The curved accent line you saw was my `border-top` + `border-radius` on `tab:checked`; that rule is deleted, so the tab is drawn exactly the way GTK draws tabs.
- **Menus are real GTK menus now.** [menu.c](src/menu.c) builds a `GtkPopoverMenu` from a `GMenu` model, with a `GSimpleActionGroup` (`settings`, `open`, `reopen`, `clear`) hung off the menu button. History is a genuine menu *submenu*, so GTK itself draws the chevron, the slide animation and the back arrow — that's why it now looks like Dolphin's submenu screenshot instead of stacked custom rows. Menu items are one line each (page title, truncated at 64 characters, falling back to the host).

![Main window](screenshots/native-main.png)

![Menu](screenshots/native-menu.png)

![History submenu](screenshots/native-history-menu.png)

**The crash is also fixed** (from the previous report, still in force): history entries no longer carry a NULL title, so pages without `<title>` can't crash the history view; and because the menu model is only rebuilt when the popover opens, activating "Clear History" never destroys the item being activated.

**Verification.** `meson compile` and a strict `-Wall -Wextra -Werror` compile are clean; `./build/indigo` launches natively with an empty log. I exercised the menu through its real actions and model: `menu.settings` → `indigo://settings`, `menu.open` → navigates to the target URL, closing a tab adds it under "Recently closed tabs", `menu.reopen(0)` opens that tab again, `menu.clear` empties the history file, and dumping the submenu model showed the expected sections/items with correct targets.

**Two things to expect:** menu labels are single-line (native menus don't do two-line rows), and the `GtkGizmo (slider) reported min width -2` lines still appear — a 40-line GTK test app reproduces them, so they come from GTK 4.22's popover scrolling, not from Indigo.
